                            <comment id="456643" author="adilger" created="Mon, 19 May 2025 19:38:37 +0000">&lt;p&gt;It looks like test_205l added by patch &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/56607" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/56607&lt;/a&gt; ("&lt;tt&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18351" title="Job stats scaling" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18351"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18351&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; obdclass: jobstat scaling&lt;/tt&gt;") has been failing intermittently since before it landed. One failure on 2024-10-11 before it landed on 2024-12-16, and then a slow burn of failures since 2924-12-19 (a few per week).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=stancheff" class="user-hover" rel="stancheff"&gt;stancheff&lt;/a&gt; could you please take a look. I don't know if this is just a test script issue, or a problem with the code itself. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="471726" author="stancheff" created="Wed, 17 Sep 2025 02:50:23 +0000">&lt;p&gt;This is a test issue, do_facet mds1 &amp;lt;blah&amp;gt; is insufficient to setup job stats and collect from all targets.&lt;br/&gt;
So sometimes all the activity is on mds2 (MDT0001 and MDT0003) and since these were not setup no jobs are found.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;CMD: onyx-142vm10 /usr/sbin/lctl set_param jobid_var=procname_uid jobid_name=%e.%u
jobid_var=procname_uid
jobid_name=%e.root
CMD: onyx-142vm10 /usr/sbin/lctl set_param mdt.*.job_cleanup_interval=5
mdt.lustre-MDT0000.job_cleanup_interval=5
mdt.lustre-MDT0002.job_cleanup_interval=5
CMD: onyx-142vm10 /usr/sbin/lctl set_param mdt.*.job_stats=clear
mdt.lustre-MDT0000.job_stats=clear
mdt.lustre-MDT0002.job_stats=clear
CMD: onyx-142vm10 /usr/sbin/lctl set_param mdt.*.job_cleanup_interval=0
mdt.lustre-MDT0000.job_cleanup_interval=0
mdt.lustre-MDT0002.job_cleanup_interval=0
CMD: onyx-142vm10 /usr/sbin/lctl get_param mdt.*.job_stats | grep job_id: | cut -d. -f2
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
